        "body": "Fathom is a San Francisco-based company, founded in 2020, that offers an AI-powered meeting notetaker for Zoom, Google Meet, and Microsoft Teams calls. The company describes its core product as capturing, transcribing, and summarizing calls automatically, with the service offered free to individual users and expanded team features available that include AI-powered CRM updates, smart action items, and call insights that flow into connected tools without manual entry. The product also includes a conversational search feature called Ask Fathom, which lets users query meeting content and receive customizable AI summaries, as well as AI Scorecards intended to surface real-time coaching moments and follow-up metrics for sales and management teams.\n\nThe held facts identify Fathom as a public company trading under the ticker FTHM with a CIK of 0001753162, and note it is registered with an MCP server under the name ai.fathom.api/mcp, described as providing AI assistants with real meeting context grounded in a user's work. The site has significant California law exposure, with 174 entries recorded under that jurisdiction, though no specific litigation cases are noted in the available data.",
